WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.778
Hi! You eat breakfast and then run off to play football, and several systems in your body are busy working together! Let's see how they share the work.

2
00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:17.826
First, the digestive system. Food goes in through the mouth and down the gullet,

3
00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:22.458
into the stomach, where it is churned and mixed with digestive juices,

4
00:00:22.608 --> 00:00:31.698
then into the small intestine, where digestion is completed. Food is broken down into simple substances that are absorbed into the blood.

5
00:00:31.848 --> 00:00:41.058
The undigested parts pass into the large intestine, which absorbs water. What is left leaves the body as faeces.

6
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:44.754
Now let's see the three systems work as a team.

7
00:00:44.904 --> 00:00:49.170
The digestive system puts digested food into the blood.

8
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.066
The respiratory system puts oxygen into the blood in the lungs.

9
00:00:54.216 --> 00:01:01.842
The circulatory system, the heart and blood vessels, carries the blood with food and oxygen all around the body.

10
00:01:01.992 --> 00:01:08.898
The body's cells use the digested food and oxygen to release energy, so we can run, jump and think.

11
00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:16.290
The carbon dioxide made by the cells is carried by the blood back to the lungs and breathed out.

12
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.834
If the digestive system doesn't work well, the blood won't have enough nutrients.

13
00:01:21.984 --> 00:01:27.354
If the respiratory system doesn't work well, the blood won't have enough oxygen.

14
00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:33.666
If the heart stops, food and oxygen can't reach the cells, and the cells can't release energy.

15
00:01:33.816 --> 00:01:41.442
During exercise, cells need more energy, so you breathe faster and your heart beats faster.

16
00:01:41.592 --> 00:01:48.978
Watch out! Some pupils say digested food is absorbed into the blood in the stomach. That's not right!

17
00:01:49.128 --> 00:01:59.010
The stomach is only part of digestion. Digestion is completed in the small intestine, and that's where digested food is mainly absorbed into the blood.

18
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:03.978
The large intestine mainly absorbs water.

19
00:02:04.128 --> 00:02:15.162
Your turn! Which system carries digested food and oxygen to cells all over the body? Pause and think.

20
00:02:15.312 --> 00:02:24.162
The circulatory system. The heart pumps blood through blood vessels to the whole body. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:24.312 --> 00:02:33.546
Another one! Which two things do cells use to release energy? Pause and think.

22
00:02:33.696 --> 00:02:42.762
Digested food and oxygen. They come from the digestive and respiratory systems. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:52.602
Last one! How does the carbon dioxide made by cells leave the body? Pause and think.

24
00:02:52.752 --> 00:02:59.418
The blood carries it to the lungs, and we breathe it out. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:59.568 --> 00:03:15.306
Remember: the digestive system turns food into nutrients absorbed in the small intestine; the respiratory system adds oxygen to the blood; the circulatory system delivers both around the body. Cells use them to release energy.

26
00:03:15.456 --> 00:03:20.826
Eat well and exercise to keep your body's team strong!

